steps.task:
Scout finding:
{previous}

Read the cited file and VERIFY the claim against the actual code. If verified, create a GitHub issue with `gh issue create` containing: root cause (file:line + snippet), impact + severity, proposed minimal fix, acceptance criteria, verification steps. Return the issue URL and number. If the claim is unverifiable or the scout returned NO_ISSUE, return exactly: SKIP

GitHub issue from planner:
{previous}

Read the issue (gh issue view <number>). Then: (1) git checkout -b fix/issue-NNN-short-desc origin/main, (2) apply the minimal verified fix, (3) verify with `uv run python -c "import ast; ast.parse(open('src/...').read())"` and `uv run python -m pytest tests/`, (4) git commit -m "fix: <summary> (closes #NNN)", (5) git push origin fix/issue-NNN-short-desc, (6) gh pr create --base main --head fix/issue-NNN-short-desc --title "fix: <summary> (closes #NNN)". Return the PR URL. Do NOT merge.

Review the PR from worker:
{previous}

Classify the risk tier from the diff: T1 (safe — bug/test/doc/refactor, tests green, no security/credential/data-model touch) → run `gh pr merge --squash --delete-branch`; T2/T3 (feature/config/security/critical) → PAUSE, report a concise summary for the human, do NOT merge; if defects are found → report findings (the worker auto-fixes in the next loop). Return the decision.
